      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this implementation, this new color will be applied in the next tick, which results in a delay of `HOOK_TICK_INTERVAL_MS`. This is not an instant transition.\n\nFor example, in the following sequence:\n```\n    color-0 {\n        led-color \u003d \u003c\u0026battery_led_amber\u003e;\n        period-ms \u003d \u003c0\u003e;\n    };\n    color-1 {\n        led-color \u003d \u003c\u0026battery_led_off\u003e;\n        period-ms \u003d \u003c500\u003e;\n    };\n    ...\n```\n\nThe color-1 (or transition to `off`) is advanced at 0ms but it is applied at 250ms (the next tick, assuming `HOOK_TICK_INTERVAL_MS` is 250ms). This is not an expected behavior that the transition to `off` should start at 0ms, instead of 250ms.\n\nThis implementation has the correct behavior only when the next color is the same as the previous one and its delay is `HOOK_TICK_INTERVAL_MS`, like:\n```\n    color-0 {\n        led-color \u003d \u003c\u0026battery_led_amber\u003e;\n        period-ms \u003d \u003c0\u003e;\n    };\n    color-1 {\n        led-color \u003d \u003c\u0026battery_led_amber\u003e;\n        period-ms \u003d \u003c250\u003e;\n    };\n    color-2 {\n        led-color \u003d \u003c\u0026battery_led_off\u003e;\n        period-ms \u003d \u003c500\u003e;\n    };\n```\n\nYou need another similar color advancing loop before applying the color, like in line 188.",
