      "writtenOn": "2025-12-17T01:22:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The LED driver is currently designed to apply the expected color on every tick even for patterns that have terminated (instead of just skipping the application for a terminated pattern).\n\nMy reasoning is because the LED policy manager is not guaranteed to be always in control of the LED. For example, if `auto_control` is turned off, there is no guarantee the color is correct when `auto_control` is turned back on. So the LED policy manager should be constantly updating with the correct information so that the LED can be restored to the proper color after any interruptions.",
      "parentUuid": "ecaa95ae_d4b41a2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 212,
